  "observations": [
    "Timestamp-only diagnostic module: the sparse subtitle packet at19999001 sets the old common start, ahead of the first retained video I-frame at9920001. That I-frame and the next at19920001 are discarded; video waits until29920001. The26-second native recording has no decoded video. The47.7-second desktop recording decodes but its video starts about9.91seconds after audio.",
    "Production OutputStartDate now computes the common start from accepted buffered audio/video streams when present. Sparse subtitles cannot advance it. Subtitle-only output retains the previous rule. Remaining OutputStart/OutputSend behavior is unchanged.",
    "Direct production calculation:8pass/3expectedfail before,11pass after. Cases cover sparse subtitles with AV/audio/multiplevideo, later audio alignment, subtitle-only, audio-only, missing DTS/PTS fallback, absent keyframes, rejected/empty streams and an empty recording.",
    "Ordinary GUI311/Core265/record322: arm paused0, Play, stop recording after28.3wallseconds while primary continues, then normal Quit. Independent FFmpeg decoding yields487video frames/19.48seconds and914audio frames/19.498667seconds. Stream starts differ0.021146seconds. App exits0/602modules/zero errors/all guards.",
    "Three actual public-API native recordings (clean, paused precise seek sequence, seek with subtitles disabled) stop normally and decode aligned AV. Each26-second recording yields431video frames/17.24seconds; audio/video starts differ0.021146seconds and durations differ0.002667seconds. Native outputs use dummy/software devices and do not replace ordinary desktop evidence."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Compressed passthrough still starts at a usable keyframe, so this long-GOP fixture omits its initial seconds. This change repairs subtitle-driven extra loss/misalignment; it does not promise frame-exact recording from the clicked time, subtitle overlap reconstruction, every codec/container or final-package acceptance.",
    "The initial native calculation test build needed MODULE_STRING and a module-name definition; r318/r319 compilation/link failures remain local with their nonzero saved results. The later cross-libtool host-path warnings are retained locally; independently staged Windows executables run successfully. No failed build is promoted to a test pass.",
    "Diagnostic module08d00995 is timestamp-only instrumentation and is not the selected ordinary module930205b1. The GUI and Core stay unchanged by this recording build. Before/after outputs and full logs remain ignored locally; only owned captures, reports, source identities and sanitized timestamp lines are retained here.",
    "Full recording preferences, all media formats, accessibility/DPI, physical devices and consolidated final-package replay remain separate beta requirements. Only generated owned media was used. Security/privacy choices were unchanged."
  ],
